===============================================================================
DEFAULT.OPTIONS — Quick Reference for External Parameters
This file is documentation only. The C program does NOT read this file.
It lists all parameters that can be modified externally (CLI or pywrap),
their flags, YAML keys, default values, and short descriptions.
===============================================================================


------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SIMULATION CONTROL OPTIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Dust drift
  CLI:       -drift
  YAML:      enable_dust_drift
  Default:   1.0
  Info:      Enable (1) or disable (0) dust radial drift.

Dust growth
  CLI:       -growth
  YAML:      enable_dust_growth
  Default:   1.0
  Info:      Enable (1) or disable (0) dust growth.

Gas evolution
  CLI:       -evol
  YAML:      enable_gas_evolution
  Default:   1.0
  Info:      Enable (1) or disable (0) gas surface density evolution.

Two-population dust model
  CLI:       -twopop
  YAML:      enable_two_dust_populations
  Default:   1.0
  Info:      Enable (1) or disable (0) the two-population dust model.

Fragmentation velocity
  CLI:       -ufrag
  YAML:      fragmentation_velocity
  Default:   1000.0
  Info:      Fragmentation threshold velocity (cm/s).

Fragmentation factor
  CLI:       -ffrag
  YAML:      fragmentation_factor
  Default:   0.37
  Info:      Scaling factor for fragmentation efficiency.


------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DISK PARAMETERS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Number of grid points
  CLI:       -n
  YAML:      number_of_grid_points
  Default:   2000
  Info:      Number of radial grid cells.

Inner radius (AU)
  CLI:       -ri
  YAML:      inner_radius_au
  Default:   1.0
  Info:      Inner boundary of the disk.

Outer radius (AU)
  CLI:       -ro
  YAML:      outer_radius_au
  Default:   100.0
  Info:      Outer boundary of the disk.

Gas surfce density at the fiducial radius (in M_sun/AU^2)
  CLI:       -sigma0_init
  YAML:      initial_gas_sigma0_msun_per_au2
  Default:   1.0
  Info:      Gas surface density at 1 AU.

Gas surface density exponent
  CLI:       -index_init
  YAML:      sigma_profile_exponent
  Default:   0.5
  Info:      Exponent p in Σ(r) ∝ r^-p.

Alpha viscosity parameter
  CLI:       -alpha_init
  YAML:      alpha_viscosity
  Default:   0.01
  Info:      Shakura–Sunyaev α parameter.

Stellar mass (M_sun)
  CLI:       -m0_init
  YAML:      star_mass_msun
  Default:   1.0
  Info:      Mass of the central star.

Aspect ratio at 1 AU
  CLI:       -h_init
  YAML:      aspect_ratio_at_1au
  Default:   0.05
  Info:      Disk scale height ratio H/R at 1 AU.

Flaring index
  CLI:       -flind_init
  YAML:      flaring_index
  Default:   0.5
  Info:      Exponent describing disk flaring.


------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEAD ZONE PARAMETERS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Inner dead-zone radius
  CLI:       -rdzei
  YAML:      deadzone_inner_radius_au
  Default:   0.0
  Info:      The inner edge of the dead zone in AU

Outer dead-zone radius
  CLI:       -rdzeo
  YAML:      deadzone_outer_radius_au
  Default:   0.0
  Info:      The outer edge of the dead zone in AU

Inner transition width multiplier
  CLI:       -drdzei
  YAML:      deadzone_inner_transition_width_mult
  Default:   0.0
  Info:      The width of the inner dead zone edge transition in local pressure scale-height units (H)

Outer transition width multiplier
  CLI:       -drdzeo
  YAML:      deadzone_outer_transition_width_mult
  Default:   0.0
  Info:      The width of the outer dead zone edge transition in local pressure scale-height units (H)

Alpha reduction inside dead zone
  CLI:       -amod
  YAML:      deadzone_alpha_reduction
  Default:   0.0
  Info:      Alpha reduction parameter in the dead zone


------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DUST PARAMETERS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Number of dust particles
  CLI:       -ndust
  YAML:      number_of_dust_particles
  Default:   5000
  Info:      Number of dust particles used to represent the dust surface density. Does NOT need to match 
             the number of gas grid cells, but it is recommended to use at least as many particles as gas cells. 
             Using fewer particles than grid cells reduces spatial resolution and can lead to noisy or poorly sampled 
             dust profiles. Using more particles is allowed and improves sampling quality.

Dust-to-gas ratio
  CLI:       -eps
  YAML:      initial_dust_to_gas_ratio
  Default:   0.01
  Info:      The initial dust-to-gas ratio in the disk.

Population 1-to-population 2 mass ratio
  CLI:       -ratio
  YAML:      population_one_mass_ratio
  Default:   0.85
  Info:      This option controlls the mass ratio of the first and the secondary (micron-sized) dust component.

Cm-sized dust component size (cm)
  CLI:       -onesize
  YAML:      one_size_particle_value_cm
  Default:   0.0
  Info:      Initial uniform size for the first dust component in cm-s.

Micro-grain size (cm)
  CLI:       -mic
  YAML:      micro_particle_size_cm
  Default:   1e-4
  Info:      The initial uniform size of the secondary (micron-sized) dust component in cm-s.

Dust material density (g/cm^3)
  CLI:       -pdensity
  YAML:      dust_particle_density_g_cm3
  Default:   1.6
  Info:      Internal density of the dust grains in g/cm^3.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TIME PARAMETERS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Fixed timestep
  CLI:       -tStep
  YAML:      fixed_time_step
  Default:   0.0
  Info:      The timestep used for time integration (in years). If set to 0, the program automatically computes a stable 
             timestep each iteration based on the CFL condition. If the user-defined timestep is larger than the CFL-limited 
             value, the code overrides it and uses the internally computed safe timestep. If the user-defined timestep is 
             smaller than the CFL value (and non-zero), the user-defined value is used.

Total simulation time
  CLI:       -tmax
  YAML:      total_simulation_time
  Default:   1e6
  Info:      End of simulation times in years.

Output frequency
  CLI:       -outfreq
  YAML:      output_write_frequency
  Default:   1000.0
  Info:      Determines how many snapshots are written during the entire simulation. The program divides the total simulation time 
             by this value to obtain the snapshot interval. For example, if tmax = 1e6 years and outfreq = 1000, snapshots are written 
             every 1000 years. Higher values produce more frequent outputs; lower values produce fewer, more widely spaced snapshots.



------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FILE I/O
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Input file
  CLI:       -i
  YAML:      input_file_path
  Default:   (empty)
  Info:      Optional initial profile file.

Output directory
  CLI:       -o
  YAML:      output_directory_name
  Default:   output
  Info:      Directory where simulation results are written.
